Calc pastes multi-line text without the Text Import dialog under LOK

Pasting text with more than one line made Calc open its Text Import
dialog for every view except a LOK mobile phone. An Ely client closes
every kernel dialog, so the import never ran and the paste failed with
"the engine did not paste" (Ely R15.27, issue #56). Under LOK the text
now imports with fixed options, as Excel pastes: tab-separated, '"'
quotes (a quoted field may hold a line break), special numbers such as
dates detected, one undo step. Setting the options selects the full
CSV reader (ExtText2Doc); the plain line reader split quoted line
breaks. The Markdown chooser in the same branch is skipped too; it
would be one more dialog the client closes.

ExtText2Doc changes, for imports into an existing sheet only (paste,
insert, Text to Columns, all with undo); whole-file imports are as
before:
- It sizes the range and clears it before writing. A line ending in a
  separator has one more, empty, field, which the sizing never
  counted, so that cell kept its old content. The sizing pass now
  counts it, unless the column info skips that column.
- It cut one trailing newline from every field, a speed workaround for
  some CSV files. A pasted quoted field such as "a<LF>" lost real
  content that way; with undo the field is kept whole.

diff --git a/sc/source/ui/docshell/impex.cxx b/sc/source/ui/docshell/impex.cxx
index 0d08d1f74..92a25889f 100644
--- a/sc/source/ui/docshell/impex.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/docshell/impex.cxx
@@ -1679,7 +1679,8 @@ bool ScImportExport::ExtText2Doc( SvStream& rStrm )
                             cStr, pSeps, bMerge, bIsQuoted, bOverflowCell, bRemoveSpace );
                     // some dodgy CSVs have a trailing linefeed in each token, which will
                     // make the code think that we have a multi-line field, which will slow things down a lot.
-                    if (aCell.endsWith("\n"))
+                    // Pasted fields keep their newlines
+                    if (!bUndo && aCell.endsWith("\n"))
                         aCell = aCell.copy(0, aCell.getLength()-1);
 
                     sal_uInt8 nFmt = SC_COL_STANDARD;
@@ -1721,6 +1722,17 @@ bool ScImportExport::ExtText2Doc( SvStream& rStrm )
                     }
                     ++nSourceCol;
                 }
+                // A trailing separator ends one more, empty, field
+                if (bDetermineRange && !bMerge && !aLine.isEmpty() && nCol <= rDoc.MaxCol()
+                    && ScGlobal::UnicodeStrChr(pSeps, aLine[aLine.getLength() - 1]))
+                {
+                    sal_uInt8 nFmt = SC_COL_STANDARD;
+                    for (i = nInfoStart; i < nInfoCount; i++)
+                        if (pColStart[i] == nSourceCol + 1)
+                            nFmt = pColFormat[i];
+                    if (nFmt != SC_COL_SKIP)
+                        ++nCol;
+                }
             }
             if (nEndCol < nCol)
                 nEndCol = nCol;     //! points to the next free or even rDoc.MaxCol()+2
